  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Construction of Family Health Houses (FHH) in Underserved Remote Rural Areas in the Helmand Province of Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Closely working with the local communities, IOM will lead the construction of 10 Family Health Housing (FHH) in Helmand based on a standardized design and layout. The FHH is a community-based health facility which aims to increase access to essential reproductive, maternal, neonatal, child and adolescent health (RMNCAH) services and bridge the gap between health post and sub-health center. UNDP will provide renewable solar energy for supply of electricity and hot water systems at the remote FHH sites. UNFPA will support and train midwives to improve their capacity to provide RMNCAH services, as well as equip the FHHs with the necessary medical and non-medical equipment, medicine, furniture, and operational cost to properly run the FHHs.</narrative>
  </description>
